{
  "_about": [
    "Hand-reviewed decisions the MD workbook import (import_md_workbook.py) cannot derive from the workbook or the seed catalog.",
    "concepts: resolution for every workbook factor name that does not match one single seed concept by exact name or by alias.",
    "  A key is the factor name as written in the workbook (matched case-insensitively) or 'Sheet name::factor name' when the",
    "  same name means different things on different tabs. Forms:",
    "    {\"existing\": \"<public_id>\", \"alias\": true}  -> use that seed or new concept; add the workbook name as a candidate alias",
    "    {\"new\": \"<public_id>\", \"name\": ..., \"type\": ..., \"category\": ..., \"aliases\": [...], \"is_a\": ..., \"narrower_than\": ...}",
    "    {\"formulation\": \"<public_id>\", \"name\": ..., \"of\": \"<substance public_id>\", \"dosage_form\": ..., \"route\": ..., \"strength_text\": ...}",
    "    {\"alternatives\": [name, name, ...]}  -> one participant per member, all in one alternative_group ('any one of these')",
    "  A seed alias that matches the name of a NEW concept is re-pointed to it (this is how combined seed concepts are split).",
    "retype: seed concepts whose concept_type/category the workbook content contradicts.",
    "reject_aliases: seed aliases that point at the wrong concept and are not re-pointed by a new concept.",
    "timing: structured timing_recommendations rows for the Tühja kõhuga / Päevaaeg cases, keyed 'Sheet::Case name'.",
    "  Only windows the MD text states plainly; the instruction text itself is always stored, these columns are the typed reading.",
    "evidence_effects: typed effect numbers for evidence rows that state them plainly, keyed 'Sheet::row', guarded by the source string."
  ],
